# C16-CTL (CONTROL): lifecycle churn at eight seats with prefix caching on, 16 sessions, on the production audited profile and base image. READ: 16 of 16 completed, no engine death, no abort, every
# release logged, the reservation hold exercised and released, captures and releases balanced, the kernel cache +0 programs. A FAIL is a production finding (as P1b-CTL). Real time ~45.
# L8-CTL and C16-CTL are two jobs, not one: their prompt lengths and answer budgets differ and a job file has one of each (and every gate arm boots its own container, so batching them would save only the reset).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-window and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window runs ONLY on today's production image: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's) and the production profile family
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_GATE_PLAN=churn
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=253920,200000,131072,65536,32768,16384,8192,4096,253920,131072,65536,32768,16384,8192,4096,1536
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=1024
C2_GATE_JIT=record
C2_GATE_AUDITS=extent
C2_GATE_SALT=fresh
